=== HINT 1 ===
malloc signature:  void *malloc(size_t size);
Cast the result:   int *p = (int *)malloc(len * sizeof(int));

=== HINT 2 ===
Always NULL-check after malloc:
  if (p == NULL) { /* handle error */ }

For this exercise, just return NULL on failure - the assert in main will catch it.

=== HINT 3 ===
free() takes the same pointer you got from malloc:
  free(p);

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
int *int_array_new(int len) {
    int *p = (int *)malloc((size_t)len * sizeof(int));
    return p;   // may be NULL - caller checks
}
void int_array_free(int *p) {
    free(p);
}
